  "content": {
    "theory": "Forms get powerful when you add **choice widgets** — radio buttons, checkboxes, dropdowns — and sensible validation.\n\n### Radio buttons (pick one)\n```html\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"plan\" value=\"free\" id=\"plan-free\">\n<label for=\"plan-free\">Free</label>\n<input type=\"radio\" name=\"plan\" value=\"pro\" id=\"plan-pro\">\n<label for=\"plan-pro\">Pro</label>\n```\nAll radios with the **same `name`** belong to one group — only one can be selected.\n\n### Checkboxes (pick many)\n```html\n<input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"topics\" value=\"dsa\" id=\"t-dsa\">\n<label for=\"t-dsa\">DSA</label>\n<input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"topics\" value=\"aptitude\" id=\"t-apt\">\n<label for=\"t-apt\">Aptitude</label>\n```\n\n### Select dropdown\n```html\n<label for=\"level\">Experience</label>\n<select name=\"level\" id=\"level\">\n  <option value=\"beginner\">Beginner</option>\n  <option value=\"intermediate\">Intermediate</option>\n  <option value=\"advanced\">Advanced</option>\n</select>\n```\n\n### Required & defaults\n```html\n<input type=\"email\" name=\"email\" required>\n<input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"terms\" checked>\n```\n\n- `required` → the browser won't submit until it's filled\n- `checked` → pre-selected by default\n\n### Putting it together\n```html\n<form>\n  <label for=\"name\">Full name</label>\n  <input type=\"text\" id=\"name\" name=\"name\" required>\n\n  <p>Level</p>\n  <input type=\"radio\" name=\"level\" value=\"beginner\" id=\"l1\">\n  <label for=\"l1\">Beginner</label>\n\n  <button type=\"submit\">Register</button>\n</form>\n```",
